# Milestone 09 — Basic Check-In Interface

- **Status:** Not started
- **Objective:** Scaffold the check-in PWA with a service worker, IndexedDB layer, QR scanning, and manual search screens so the device can identify a student (vertical slice 2 begins).
- **Dependencies:** 01 (Project foundation), 02 (Shared types and validation)

## Included work
- `apps/check-in-pwa` vanilla TypeScript + Web Components application.
- Web app manifest and service worker for installability and offline shell.
- IndexedDB repository layer: stores for `students`, `classes`, `schedules`, `enrollments`, `events`, `meta` (sync state, device token).
- QR scanning screen using `@zxing/browser` with fallback to `jsQR`.
- External keyboard-scanner support (rapid keystrokes + Enter).
- Manual student search screen (debounced prefix search over local roster).
- Manual student ID entry screen.
- Student identification result screen (name, ID, class info placeholder).
- Connectivity status indicator.
- Minimal, accessible, large-touch-target UI with portrait/landscape support.
- No cloud fonts; system/bundled fonts only.
- Unit tests for the IndexedDB layer and search.

## Explicitly excluded work
- No attendance session creation / time-in (deferred to M10).
- No sync to main computer (deferred to M12/M13).
- No device pairing (deferred to M26).
- No parent acknowledgment (deferred to M18+).
- No checkout (deferred to M21).
- No desktop UI (deferred to M14+).

